{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>A just balance and scales</b> — they are one matter, and the pocket-stones are from Him, like 'for it is He who commanded to act with weight and scales,' according to the rule, and the function of the balance belongs to Him." "<b>All the stones of a bag</b> — because the shekel is twenty gerah, and the sense is that there be none large or small there; 'are YHWH's' — they are His, and the sense: for He desires them."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:08.647855409Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}